+# Sovereign TIDES (SOV-P-002 W12), src/datum_lzt1.[ch]:
+#
+#   Persisted identity. datum.identity_key_file (string, default "") names a
+#   file holding the DATUM identity keys (the ed25519 key of the handshake
+#   hello plus the x25519 pair, i.e. local_datum_keys). Missing: new keys are
+#   generated and written with O_CREAT|O_EXCL, mode 0600. Present: loaded;
+#   the gateway refuses to start (DLOG_FATAL, exit 1) if the file is group- or
+#   world-accessible, not a regular file, or malformed (including key halves
+#   that do not re-derive from the seeds). Format, text, five lines:
+#       datum-identity-v1
+#       ed25519_pk <64 hex>
+#       ed25519_sk <128 hex>     (libsodium form: seed || pk)
+#       x25519_pk  <64 hex>      (one space after the name)
+#       x25519_sk  <64 hex>
+#   Unset: a fresh key every start, as stock.
+#
+#   LZT1 template attestations. datum.lzt1_attest (bool, default true), live
+#   only with a persisted identity key (otherwise one WARN at startup and
+#   nothing is emitted or reserved). Per pooled job, every coinbase variant
+#   built from the coinbaser (types 1-5, and type 0 = copy of type 4) gets one
+#   zero-value output, inserted right before the witness commitment:
+#       OP_RETURN PUSH68 "LZT1" BLAKE2b-256(A) G     (70-byte script, 79 bytes)
+#   G = the identity ed25519 key. A (185 bytes) is datum-wire authorship.rs:
+#   v=1 | G | height | prev (internal order, as the job section) |
+#   BLAKE2b-256(the job's merkle branches as sent to Prime) | sum of the
+#   variant's output values | n_tx (template txs + 1) | mempool_digest (zero)
+#   | node_tag (zero) | t_gbt (job creation time, unix ms) | payout_digest
+#   (SHA256d of compactsize(n-1) || every other output, in final order).
+#   A is computed from the serialized coinbase (coinb1 || 12 zero bytes ||
+#   coinb2, exactly what Prime assembles) and the id is written into coinb2.
+#   79 bytes per variant are added to each variant's fixed byte budget
+#   (cb_req_sz), so the size/weight fit and the per-type caps account for it.
+#   On SHA256d jobs a variant whose extranonce sits in an OP_RETURN output
+#   (type 2 always; all types if the scriptSig is too long) varies per share
+#   and is left unattested. BLAKE2b jobs zero that slot, so all are attested.
+#   Before a job is released (coinbaser thread, before need_coinbaser=false)
+#   the gateway sends, via datum_protocol_mining_cmd, one 253-byte message
+#       0x5A | datum job id | coinbase id | A | ed25519 sig | 0xFE
+#   per published variant (BLAKE2b: blake2b_coinbase_index only; SHA256d: all
+#   attested variants). sig = crypto_sign_detached over
+#   "XBT-SOVEREIGN-TIDES/1\0" || A. Setting DATUM_LZT1_DUMP=<file> appends,
+#   per variant, the arguments of prime's lzt1_check
+#   (<msg> <coinbase> <prev> <G> <branches...>).
+#
+#   XBT-NTA coinbaser shape. datum_coinbaser_v2_parse also accepts a script of
+#   exactly 70 bytes starting 6a 44 'N' 'T' 'A' 02 with value 0; the output
+#   buffer grows to 70. Any other script over 64 bytes still voids the list.
+#
